==English==

===Alternative forms===
* {{alter|en|datagramme}}

===Etymology===
From {{suffix|en|data|gram}}.

===Pronunciation===
* {{audio|en|en-uk-datagram.ogg|a=UK}}

===Noun===
{{en-noun}}

# {{lb|en|networking}} A [[packet]] of [[data]] passed across a [[network]].
#* {{RQ:RFC|768|title= User Datagram Protocol|author=w:Jon Postel|date=28 August 1980|passage=The pseudo  header  conceptually prefixed to the UDP header contains the source  address,  the destination  address,  the protocol,  and the  UDP length. This information gives protection against misrouted '''datagrams'''.}}

====Usage notes====
* Although the specifications of the [[Internet Protocol]] say that datagrams are what pass through the network, the word ''packet'' is more commonly used.

