#* {{quote-journal|en|year=1981|month=October|author=Alfred R. Dixon Jr.|title=Data Base Management|editor=Terry Tufts|journal=The Harvest|volume=3|issue=2|location=Arlington Heights, Ill.|publisher=Northern Illinois Apple Users Group|page=13|pageurl=https://archive.org/details/theharvest3.2/page/n12/mode/1up|column=1|oclc=13287523|passage=The Modifiable Data Base is a very nice system and is, generally, highly recommended* It is memory dependent and, once formated,{{sic}} ('''datagrammed''') is not changeable.}}
#* {{quote-newsgroup|en|date=31 July 1992|author=Dave Pierson|title=Uploads to wuarchive.wustl.edu|newsgroup=rec.railroad|archiveurl=https://web.archive.org/web/20250605182809/https://groups.google.com/g/rec.railroad/c/KjZPE1eoHOI/m/ojsv4loXUTYJ|passage=>* How does the dispatch station know where the trains are? Is it<br>>just by the engineer notifying them, or is it done by some computerized<br>>system in the track?<br>Varies. Most common is by track circuits, in which the train indicates occupancy of a "block" by shorting the rails together. This gets "'''datagrammed'''" to the CTC center. (short hand, simplified description).}}
#* {{quote-newsgroup|en|date=30 October 1999|author=Decklin Foster|title=[haiku] nyc right about now.|newsgroup=alt.teens.poetry.and.stuff|archiveurl=https://web.archive.org/web/20250605182819/https://groups.google.com/g/alt.teens.poetry.and.stuff/c/cA7rVPbOadk/m/MWBDddboycYJ|passage=the crowd mills about '''datagrammed''' packets flowing without words to say.}}